COMMON PARK ELEMENTS
After reviewing the three park concepts with City Staff, the design team revised
the design into two park alternatives to share with the public at an open house
event. The character images above depict the program and design elements
featured in both options.
Another key park feature included in both alternates is a berm. While this is
seamlessly integrated into the park design of both alternates, it provides the
residential neighborhood to the north protection from future flooding within
the Dry Creek corridor.
